From: Bharat Dintakurti <bdintakurti@nvidia.com>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 22:49:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] NVIDIA: SAUCE: ACPI: processor_idle: Clear freed cpuidle
 device pointers

BugLink: https://bugs.launchpad.net/bugs/2167301

acpi_processor_power_init() publishes each allocated cpuidle device through
the per-CPU acpi_cpuidle_device pointer. The normal processor power-exit
path and the global power-state refresh path unregister and free that
device without clearing the published pointer.

If reinitialization fails before installing a replacement, the per-CPU slot
continues to reference freed memory. A repeated or adjacent lifecycle
operation can then consume the dangling pointer.

Clear the owner slot immediately after unregistering the device and before
freeing it in both paths.

Fixes: e18afcb7b2a12 ("ACPI: processor_idle: Fix memory leak in acpi_processor_power_exit()")
Fixes: 07cba0de5598 ("ACPI: processor: idle: Reset cpuidle on C-state list changes")
Signed-off-by: Bharat Dintakurti <bdintakurti@nvidia.com>
Signed-off-by: Ishan Shah <ishah@nvidia.com>
Reviewed-by: Ishan Shah <ishah@nvidia.com>
Assisted-by: OpenAI-Codex:gpt-5.6
Acked-by: Jamie Nguyen <jamien@nvidia.com>
Acked-by: Carol L Soto <csoto@nvidia.com>
Acked-by: Nirmoy Das <nirmoyd@nvidia.com>
Signed-off-by: Brad Figg <bfigg@nvidia.com>
Ledger-Change: C-02107
Ledger-Origin: nvidia-bos@f1c221c6226c943a77996d03eb2fcfd1dbe58e25
---
 drivers/acpi/processor_idle.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/acpi/processor_idle.c b/drivers/acpi/processor_idle.c
index e113bcbbb882..b7edcf21a503 100644
--- a/drivers/acpi/processor_idle.c
+++ b/drivers/acpi/processor_idle.c
@@ -1054,6 +1054,7 @@ int acpi_processor_power_state_has_changed(struct acpi_processor *pr)
 				continue;
 
 			cpuidle_unregister_device_no_lock(dev);
+			per_cpu(acpi_cpuidle_device, cpu) = NULL;
 			kfree(dev);
 			_pr->flags.power = 0;
 		}
@@ -1196,6 +1197,7 @@ void acpi_processor_power_exit(struct acpi_processor *pr)
 
 	if (pr->flags.power) {
 		cpuidle_unregister_device(dev);
+		per_cpu(acpi_cpuidle_device, pr->id) = NULL;
 		kfree(dev);
 	}
 
